  "prefLabel": "Rev 414.01 Exemption for the Blind",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 414.01 Exemption for the Blind.\n\n(a) An applicant shall not be entitled to the exemption for the blind pursuant to RSA 72:37 unless:\n\n(1) The applicant’s residential real estate is located in a municipality that has adopted the exemption for the blind pursuant to RSA 72:27-a; and\n\n(2) The applicant is eligible pursuant to this part.\n\n(b) The exemption for the blind shall be prorated, if applicable pursuant to RSA 72:41, and deducted from the assessed value of an entitled applicant’s residential real estate.\n\nSource. #12027, eff 10-28-16; renumbered by #12925 (formerly Rev 413.01); ss by #13943-B, eff 4-27-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev400.html"
